      "RWW",
      "[Expert R1] (Detect atomicity violations in the code.)\n```json\n{\n    \"violations\": [\n        {\n            \"sharedVariable\": \"data\",\n            \"accessPattern\": [\"Read\", \"Write\", \"Write\"],\n            \"lines\": [8, 17, 9]\n        },\n        {\n            \"sharedVariable\": \"data\",\n            \"accessPattern\": [\"Read\", \"Write\", \"Write\"],\n            \"lines\": [16, 9, 17]\n        }\n    ]\n}\n```\n\n[System] Expert first round completed in 4.53 seconds\n\n[Judge R1] (Validate the expert's defect report and check control/interrupt conditions.)\nLet me analyze each read/write operation for the global variable `data` to determine if they can be executed.\n\n## Analysis of Read/Write Operations\n\n### 1. Operations in svp_simple_304_001_isr_1 (lines 8-9)\n- **Line 8**: `int tmp = data + 1;` - This is a **Read** operation on `data`\n- **Line 9**: `data = tmp;` - This is a **Write** operation on `data`\n\nThese operations are not guarded by any control conditions. Since this is an interrupt handler (ISR1), it can be triggered by the system at any time when interrupts are enabled.\n\n### 2. Operations in svp_simple_304_001_isr_2 (lines 16-17)\n- **Line 16**: `int tmp = data + 2;` - This is a **Read** operation on `data`\n- **Line 17**: `data = tmp;` - This is a **Write** operation on `data`\n\nThese operations are not guarded by any control conditions. Since this is an interrupt handler (ISR2), it can be triggered by the system at any time when interrupts are enabled.\n\n### 3. Operations in svp_simple_304_001_isr_3 (lines 23-24)\n- **Line 23**: `if (data >= 3)` - This is a **Read** operation on `data` (used in the condition)\n- **Line 24**: `reach_error();abort();` - This is executed when `data >= 3`\n\nThe control condition is `data >= 3`. Since `data` is initialized to 0 and can be modified by ISRs 1 and 2 (which increment it by 1 and 2 respectively), this condition can be satisfied when the cumulative effect of these ISRs results in `data >= 3`.\n\n### 4. Operations in svp_simple_304_001_main (lines 31-32)\n- **Line 31**: `return 0;` - No operations on `data`\n\n## Summary of Analysis\n\nAll read/write operations on `data` can be executed:\n- The read/write operations in ISR1 (lines 8, 9) can execute when ISR1 is triggered\n- The read/write operations in ISR2 (lines 16, 17) can execute when ISR2 is triggered\n- The read operation in ISR3 (line 23) can execute when ISR3 is triggered\n- The condition `data >= 3` can be satisfied through the cumulative effect of ISR1 and ISR2\n\nSince all interrupts can preempt each other based on their priorities (ISR3 has highest priority 3, ISR2 has priority 2, ISR1 has priority 1), all the reported atomicity violations are valid.\n\n```json\n{\n    \"violations\": [\n        {\n            \"sharedVariable\": \"data\",\n            \"accessPattern\": [\"Read\", \"Write\", \"Write\"],\n            \"lines\": [8, 17, 9]\n        },\n        {\n            \"sharedVariable\": \"data\",\n            \"accessPattern\": [\"Read\", \"Write\", \"Write\"],\n            \"lines\": [16, 9, 17]\n        }\n    ]\n}\n```\n\n[Expert R2] (Refine the report based on judge feedback, re-check for missed or false defects.)\n```json\n{\n    \"violations\": [\n        {\n            \"sharedVariable\": \"data\",\n            \"accessPattern\": [\"Read\", \"Write\", \"Write\"],\n            \"lines\": [8, 17, 9]\n        },\n        {\n            \"sharedVariable\": \"data\",\n            \"accessPattern\": [\"Read\", \"Write\", \"Write\"],\n            \"lines\": [16, 9, 17]\n        }\n    ]\n}\n```\n\n"
